---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="How Do You Prepare for Kindergarten? | Marietta Childcare"
  description="Learn about Marietta Childcare's transition support, kindergarten readiness, and parent resources.">
  <section class="relative py-32 overflow-hidden w-screen -ml-[calc((100vw-100%)/2)]">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 z-0">
      <img 
        src="/images/Background_Images/girl_reading_book_quiet_corner_background.jpg" 
        alt="Kindergarten preparation" 
        class="w-full h-full object-cover"
      />
      <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-black/40"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="relative z-10 max-w-[1280px] mx-auto px-6 lg:px-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black mb-6 text-white drop-shadow-lg">How Do You Prepare for Kindergarten?</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mb-12 max-w-2xl text-white drop-shadow-md">Transition support, kindergarten readiness activities, and parent resources for school success.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-20 px-6 lg:px-20">
    <div class="max-w-[1280px] mx-auto">
      <article class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
        
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">Marietta Childcare prepares children for kindergarten success through intentional curriculum and support. Marietta Childcare's transition support helps children develop confidence and readiness for school.</p>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Kindergarten Readiness Skills</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare focuses on developing kindergarten readiness skills. Kindergarten readiness at Marietta Childcare includes academic skills like letter recognition and number concepts. Marietta Childcare's curriculum emphasizes social-emotional skills essential for school success.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare develops executive function skills including attention, memory, and self-control. Kindergarten readiness at Marietta Childcare includes communication skills and following directions. Marietta Childcare's comprehensive approach ensures children are prepared for kindergarten demands.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Academic Preparation</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare's curriculum includes pre-academic skills for kindergarten. Academic preparation at Marietta Childcare includes phonemic awareness, letter recognition, and early writing. Marietta Childcare teaches number concepts, counting, and early math skills.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare's literacy program prepares children for reading instruction. Literacy activities at Marietta Childcare include story time, letter activities, and writing experiences. Marietta Childcare's academic focus supports children's transition to formal schooling.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Social-Emotional Preparation</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare emphasizes social-emotional skills for kindergarten success. Social-emotional preparation at Marietta Childcare includes cooperation, sharing, and conflict resolution. Marietta Childcare teaches children to follow classroom rules and routines.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare develops children's ability to separate from parents and adjust to new environments. Social skills at Marietta Childcare include making friends and working with peers. Marietta Childcare's social-emotional curriculum builds children's confidence for kindergarten.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Classroom Routines and Expectations</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare teaches classroom routines similar to kindergarten. Classroom routines at Marietta Childcare include circle time, transitions, and independent work. Marietta Childcare's structured schedule prepares children for school day expectations.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare teaches children to follow multi-step directions. Expectations at Marietta Childcare include sitting for group activities and raising hands. Marietta Childcare's routine-based approach helps children adjust to kindergarten structure.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Self-Care and Independence Skills</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare develops self-care and independence skills. Self-care skills at Marietta Childcare include toileting, handwashing, and eating independently. Marietta Childcare teaches children to manage belongings and follow personal care routines.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare encourages independence in problem-solving and decision-making. Independence skills at Marietta Childcare include managing frustration and asking for help appropriately. Marietta Childcare's focus on independence prepares children for kindergarten self-sufficiency.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Transition Activities and Visits</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare facilitates kindergarten transitions through special activities. Transition activities at Marietta Childcare may include visits to kindergarten classrooms. Marietta Childcare's transition support helps children become familiar with their new school.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare provides resources to families about kindergarten preparation. Transition information at Marietta Childcare includes tips for supporting children at home. Marietta Childcare's transition support extends beyond the classroom to family involvement.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Parent Resources and Support</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare provides families with kindergarten preparation resources. Parent resources at Marietta Childcare include information about kindergarten readiness. Marietta Childcare offers guidance on supporting children's transition at home.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare communicates with families about their child's readiness for kindergarten. Parent conferences at Marietta Childcare discuss kindergarten preparation and next steps. Marietta Childcare's partnership with families supports successful transitions.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Developmental Assessment</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare assesses children's kindergarten readiness. Developmental assessment at Marietta Childcare uses observation and standardized tools. Marietta Childcare identifies areas of strength and areas needing additional support.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare shares assessment results with families. Assessment information at Marietta Childcare helps families understand their child's readiness. Marietta Childcare's assessment approach supports individualized transition planning.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="mb-12">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Collaboration with Schools</h2>
          <p>Marietta Childcare collaborates with local kindergarten programs. School collaboration at Marietta Childcare includes sharing information about children's development. Marietta Childcare's partnerships with schools support smooth transitions.</p>
          <p>Marietta Childcare provides transition information to kindergarten teachers. Information sharing at Marietta Childcare includes children's strengths, interests, and needs. Marietta Childcare's collaborative approach ensures continuity of care and education.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="bg-blue-50 p-6 rounded-lg mb-12">
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Prepare Your Child for Success</h3>
          <p class="mb-4">Marietta Childcare is committed to preparing children for kindergarten success. Contact Marietta Childcare to learn more about kindergarten readiness and transition support.</p>
          <a href="/contact" class="inline-block bg-blue-600 text-white px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-blue-700 transition">Contact Us</a>
        </section>

        <nav class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-4">Related Pages</h3>
          <ul class="space-y-2">
            <li><a href="/faq/curriculum" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">What's Your Curriculum?</a></li>
            <li><a href="/faq/parent-communication" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">How Do You Communicate with Parents?</a></li>
            <li><a href="/programs" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">Our Programs</a></li>
            <li><a href="/solutions/transition-to-school" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">Transition to School Support</a></li>
            <li><a href="/contact" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800">Contact Marietta Childcare</a></li>
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
